# The ordinal rank of every layer in `F`: the order in which a fusion may be evaluated. One row
# per layer, `rank` 0 where nothing lies beneath it and NULL where its descent reaches a cycle.
#
# What well-foundedness gives you
#   A well-founded relation has a rank function, `rank(x) = sup{rank(y)+1 : y R x}`, and the
#   precondition that *no name expands to itself* is the guarantee that one exists. A cycle is
#   exactly the case where it does not, which is what "no order exists in which to evaluate the
#   stack" means.
#
# Rank is the evaluation order, and `depth` is not
#   composition/descent.sqlc's `depth` is per path; the rank is the maximum over all paths. A
#   layer reachable at depth 1 and at depth 2 must not be evaluated until both arrivals are
#   ready, so a walk that evaluates in depth order can compute a fusion before one of its parts
#   exists. The minimum and the maximum differ exactly where a layer is reached by paths of two
#   lengths, a jagged partition, and checks/jagged_layer is the same phenomenon in the other
#   algebra.
#
# A cycle has no rank
#   Where a descent reaches a cycle the supremum does not exist, for the layers on it and every
#   layer above them, so those get NULL, never the depth the cycle guard happened to stop at.
#   checks/layers_move_together reports the cycle.
#
# A window, not a second walk
#   composition/descent.sqlc has already done the recursion, so the rank is one aggregate over
#   its closure.
#   Proposing another recursive CTE for this is proposing to recompute something the data already
#   carries.
#
# Carried into two artifacts
#   `examples/diagramming/main.rs` writes it into each filing's lane, and
#   `examples/graphs/main.rs` writes it into the corpus-wide layer graph's, through
#   `rank/graph_nodes.sqlc`.
#
# An emitter must write the rank
#   An emitter that writes no rank leaves the renderer its own sentinel to draw, and this relation
#   gives either a rank of at least 0 or NULL, so a negative rank on a page is a value the model
#   cannot produce. Every lane count stays exact through that, which is why it is the emitter's
#   obligation and not a count's.
#
-- composition/descent.sqlc aggregated to the deepest arrival under each layer.
SELECT l.filing, l.layer,
       CASE WHEN coalesce(bool_or(d.is_cycle), false) THEN NULL
            ELSE coalesce(max(d.depth), 0) END AS rank,
       count(d.filing)           AS arrivals
FROM      (
    :compose(layers/every_layer.sqlc)
) l
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(composition/descent.sqlc)
) d ON d.root_filing = l.filing AND d.root_layer = l.layer
GROUP BY l.filing, l.layer
